s:
The law establishes the rules concerning:
citizenship, civic rights, and the fundamental guarantees granted to citizens for the exercise of public freedoms, freedom, pluralism, and the independence of the media;
the obligations imposed by national defense on citizens in their person and property;
nationality, legal status and capacity of persons, matrimonial property regimes, inheritance, and gifts;
the procedure by which customs and traditions are established and brought into harmony with the fundamental principles of the Constitution;
the definition of crimes and offenses, as well as the penalties applicable to them, criminal procedure, and amnesty;
the organization of judicial, administrative, and financial courts, as well as the procedure followed before these courts;
the status of judges, ministerial officers, and court officers;
the general status of the civil service;
the status of the Prefectoral Corps;
the status of the Diplomatic Corps;
the status of the personnel of local authorities;
the status of the military;
the status of the personnel of the National Police;
the basis, rate, and methods of collection of taxes of all kinds;
the currency issuance system;
the electoral system for Parliament and local assemblies;
the methods of public management of economic and social activities;
the creation of categories of public institutions;
the general organization of the administration;
the state of siege and the state of emergency;
the conditions for the promotion and development of national languages.

The law determines the fundamental principles of:
education and scientific research;
the organization of national defense;
property law, real rights, and civil and commercial obligations;
labor law, trade union law, and social institutions;
the alienation and management of state and local government property;
the transfer of enterprises from the public to the private sector;
mutual aid and savings;
environmental protection and sustainable development;
the organization of production;
the system of political parties and the status of the political opposition;
the system of transportation and telecommunications;
the system of state revenues and expenditures;
the programming of objectives for state economic and social action;
the organization and functioning of public authorities.

The Superior Council of the Magistracy:
examines all matters relating to the independence of the judiciary and the ethics of judges;
makes proposals for the appointment of judges to the Court of Cassation, the Council of State, and the Court of Auditors, as well as the First Presidents of the Courts of Appeal and the Presidents of the Courts of First Instance;
gives its approval for the appointment, transfer, and promotion of judges;
adjudicates disciplinary matters concerning judges and public prosecutors.
